Based on the analysis of the provided scene images, here is the RDF representation in Turtle format alongside identified safety risks.

Scene Description in RDF Triples (Turtle Format)
```turtle
@prefix : <http://cecs571.csulb.edu/ontology/cornercase#> .
@prefix xsd: <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .

:scene1 a :Scene ;
    :scenarioName "Nighttime scene with obstacles" ;
    :hasCornerCaseType :cc1 .

:cc1 a :BehaviorAnomaly ;
    :hasActor :actor1, :actor2 ;
    :hasWeatherCondition :weather1 ;
    :hasRisk :risk1, :risk2 .

:actor1 a :Pedestrian ;  # Pedestrian running
:actor2 a :Obstacle ;     # Soccer ball on road

:weather1 a :NightCondition .

:risk1 a :PedestrianCollisionRisk ;
    :description "Risk of colliding with pedestrian" ;
    :hasSeverityScore :sev1 .

:risk2 a :RollingBallIndicator ;
    :description "Risk of colliding with rolling ball" ;
    :hasSeverityScore :sev2 .

:sev1 a :SeverityScore ;
    :severityValue "0.90"^^xsd:float .

:sev2 a :SeverityScore ;
    :severityValue "0.70"^^xsd:float .
```

Identified Risks for each risk class
